    "title": "pandas.DataFrame.keys — pandas 2.3.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.DataFrame.keys#\n\n- DataFrame.keys()[source]#\n- Get the ‘info axis’ (see Indexing for more). This is index for Series, columns for DataFrame. \n  - Returns:\n    - Index\n    - Info axis.\n Examples >>> d = pd.DataFrame(data={'A': [1, 2, 3], 'B': [0, 4, 8]}, ... index=['a', 'b', 'c']) >>> d A B a 1 0 b 2 4 c 3 8 >>> d.keys() Index(['A', 'B'], dtype='object')",
